Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. The export contains
overlapping pages, so count each report ID once. The desk merged those reports into #4471
by subject; that merge did not mean they all had the same cause.

Use each report's tenant configuration and channel to identify the cause. The intake tag is
only a guess and does not reliably identify the failure. The table below computes the counts
from the export and shows how the desk's current rules place each group.

<Callout>
Known incident. The merged ticket contains two distinct date-parsing problems and needs two
engineering issues.
</Callout>

## Cause 1: the shared parser flips day-first dates

Tenants whose locale writes the day before the month are affected when a date reaches the
shared parser. The parser reads the month first, so day and month trade places. This group
includes app and email reports, plus form reports that do not use the conflicting v3 form.
Tracked in [issue #1](https://github.com/spamowaskrzynkamailowa-ship-it/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

## Cause 2: the v3 form contradicts day-first tenants

The v3 form displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while these tenants use a day-first locale. A person
following the form's hint can submit a date that the tenant-side parser reads in the opposite
order. These form reports are a separate problem from the shared-parser failures above.
Tracked in [issue #2](https://github.com/spamowaskrzynkamailowa-ship-it/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Engineering outcome

The desk closed #4471 on 5 October. Engineering fixed the shared parser with
`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The v3-form issue will not be fixed because
`booking-v3` was retired.

